t4. the two directions a validation claim is quantified over
    domain swept: W in 0..=69, 70 declarations
    the independently written rule: admissible iff 1 <= W <= 64

defect                                         under    over                   caught by
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
none (control)                                     0       0                     nothing
under-refusal: admits W = 0                        1       0          compile-fail suite
under-refusal: admits W = 65, 66                   2       0          compile-fail suite
over-refusal: refuses the top rung W = 64          0       1     these-all-compile suite
over-refusal: refuses W = 33..35                   0       3     these-all-compile suite

reading:
  A compile-fail suite observes the under-refusal rows and is blind to the
  over-refusal rows. A these-all-compile suite is blind the other way. Neither
  shape observes both, and only a sweep against a separately written predicate
  does, because only the predicate knows which widths SHOULD have compiled.

  The over-refusal rows are the ones with no natural test author: a consumer
  who never wrote W = 34 never files a bug, and the suite stays green because
  every declaration it contains is one somebody thought of.
